.TH PAKU 1 2026-11-22 "paku 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
paku \- a small package-management wrapper around an AUR helper and pacman
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B paku
.I subcommand
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B paku
.RB [ \-\-help | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B paku
gives everyday package management on Arch Linux and its derivatives a smaller set of subcommands.
It uses an AUR helper,
.BR paru (8),
.BR yay (8)
or
.BR pikaur (1),
so the AUR is included: the one chosen (see
.BR CONFIGURATION ),
or else the first of them on the PATH, in that order. Below,
.B paru
stands for the helper in use. Without one,
.BR pacman (8),
with
.BR sudo (8)
for the operations that change the system (not when run as root), and the official repositories only.
Commands run directly, never through a shell, and
.B paku
exits with their exit code.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.BR upgrade ", " up
.B paru \-Syu
(or
.BR "sudo pacman \-Syu" ),
then
.B flatpak upgrade
if flatpak is installed and the system upgrade succeeded.
.TP
.BR maintain ", " cu ", " full ", " full\-upgrade " [" \fIargs\fR ...]
Runs
.B cachy\-update
(or
.BR arch\-update )
with the arguments.
.TP
.BR check ", " co
Lists pending updates:
.B cachy\-update \-\-list
or
.B arch\-update \-\-list
when installed, otherwise
.B paru \-Qu
(without paru,
.BR checkupdates ,
else
.BR "pacman \-Qu" ).
.TP
.BR update ", " refresh
.B paru \-Sy
(or
.BR "sudo pacman \-Sy" ).
.TP
.BR search ", " s " " \fIpkg\fR ...
.B paru \-Ss
(or
.BR "pacman \-Ss" ).
.TP
.BR install ", " add ", " i " " \fIpkg\fR ...
.B paru \-S
(or
.BR "sudo pacman \-S" ).
.TP
.BR remove ", " rm ", " uninstall " " \fIpkg\fR ...
.B paru \-Rns
(or
.BR "sudo pacman \-Rns" ).
.TP
.BR info " " \fIpkg\fR ...
.B paru \-Si
(or
.BR "pacman \-Si" ,
then
.B pacman \-Qi
if the package is not in the repositories).
.TP
.BR owns " " \fIfile\fR ...
.BR "pacman \-Qo" .
.TP
.BR files " " \fIpkg\fR ...
.BR "pacman \-Ql" .
.TP
.BR list ", " explicit
.BR "pacman \-Qe" .
.TP
.BR aur ", " aur\-list
.BR "pacman \-Qm" .
.TP
.BR aur\-audit ", " aur\-sec ", " aur\-security
Fetches the Arch Linux AUR compromised-package list with
.B curl
and checks the installed foreign packages against it.
.TP
.B clean
.B paru \-Sc
(or
.BR "sudo pacman \-Sc" ).
.TP
.BR autoremove ", " orphans
Removes the orphans
.RB ( "pacman \-Qdtq" )
with
.B \-Rns.
.TP
.BR completions " " bash | zsh | fish
Prints the completion script for the shell.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The helper comes from the
.B PAKU_HELPER
environment variable or, without it, from a
.B helper
line in the config file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
# auto, paru, yay, pikaur or pacman
helper = yay
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B auto
(the default, also with no file) takes the first helper installed, in the order paru, yay, pikaur, and
pacman without any.
.B pacman
uses pacman even when a helper is installed. A chosen helper that isn't installed, or an unknown value,
gets a warning on stderr and counts as
.BR auto .
Only the subcommands that run the package tool read the setting.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PAKU_HELPER
The helper, as in the config file; it wins over the file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/paku/config
The config file
.RI ( ~/.config/paku/config
when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset or not absolute). Lines are
.IR "key = value" ,
the value may be quoted, and
.B #
starts a comment.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit code of the command run. 1 with no subcommand, an unknown one or a missing argument;
.B aur\-audit
exits 1 when an installed package is on the list or the list can't be fetched.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR paru (8),
.BR yay (8),
.BR pikaur (1),
.BR pacman (8),
.BR checkupdates (8)
